{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":240046,"duration_api_ms":239626,"num_turns":13,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"833c3eff-299e-40df-89e6-7abc65e5e7d0","total_cost_usd":0.9618227500000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":60020,"cache_read_input_tokens":285691,"output_tokens":10941,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":60020,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":11,"outputTokens":12791,"cacheReadInputTokens":311298,"cacheCreationInputTokens":77815,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.9618227500000001,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"evidence":["The quadratic charge-balance equation (line 97) was re-derived and is mathematically correct: Alk*H^2 + Ka1*(Alk-DIC)*H + Ka1*Ka2*(Alk-2*DIC) = 0.","Unit conversions are correct: dic_mol_per_l = mg_c_total/12000/volume_l (line 46), alk_eq_per_l = meq_total/1000/volume_l (line 47), bicarbonate_mg_total = hco3_mmol_per_l * 61.0 * volume_l (line 119).","State contract (lines 13-38) correctly keeps DIC and alkalinity as explicit state and derives CO2(aq), HCO3-, CO3--, pH — matching existing WaterState fields confirmed in water.rs:10-30.","Update order (lines 123-136) is clear: all DIC/alkalinity mutations first, then one shared resolve, then read-only consumers.","Intentional exclusions (lines 150-158) are explicit and the list is comprehensive (gas exchange, other buffers, precipitation, ionic-strength, spatial layering, source-water pH).","pKa1 temperature coefficient verified against Harned & Davis (1943) formula: pK1 = 3404.71/T_K + 0.032786*T_K - 14.8435 yields d(pK1)/dT = -0.005515 per °C at 25°C, not -0.0238.","At 15°C: Harned & Davis gives pK1 = 6.4195, design note's linear approximation gives 6.59 (error = +0.17). At 35°C: H&D gives 6.3084, linear gives 6.114 (error = -0.19).","UNITS.md correctly adds _mmol_per_l pattern (line 24) and carbonate solver exception in storage rules (lines 49-52).","scientific_inventory.md entries for DIC (line 24), alkalinity (line 27), bicarbonate (line 30), and pH (line 31) all reference carbonate_state_contract.md and accurately distinguish current runtime behavior from the approved replacement.","scientific_specs.md v0.3 section (lines 169-174) references the design note and correctly describes the approved solver approach.","Prior docs_validation stage returned outcome='approved' with empty evidence, findings, and follow-up arrays — a rubber-stamp review that missed the temperature coefficient error."],"findings_or_gaps":["CRITICAL: pKa1 temperature coefficient is wrong by ~4.3x. Line 79 states pKa1(T) = 6.352 - 0.0238*(T-25). The correct slope from Harned & Davis (1943) is -0.00552/°C, not -0.0238/°C. At the temperature extremes of the stated 15-35°C range, pKa1 errors reach 0.17-0.19 units, far exceeding the document's own ±0.05 pH accuracy target (line 140). This means an implementer following the design note verbatim would produce a solver that gives wrong pH values at any temperature other than 25°C — directly violating the acceptance criterion that implementation can proceed without re-litigating fundamentals.","MINOR: The pH 7.0 fallback for near-zero alkalinity (line 110) is physically incorrect for water containing CO2 (should be acidic, ~pH 5.6 in atmospheric equilibrium), though the note transparently acknowledges this is a stability guard, not a physical model. Acceptable for first pass.","MINOR: The pKa2 fixed value of 10.33 (line 80) is correct at 25°C. The note says the solver interface should keep both constants explicit for later temperature correction — good forward-compatibility design."],"follow_up_or_amendments":["Replace the linear pKa1 approximation on line 79 with either: (a) the correct linear slope: pKa1(T) ≈ 6.352 - 0.0055*(T-25), or preferably (b) the full Harned & Davis formula: pK1 = 3404.71/(T_C + 273.15) + 0.032786*(T_C + 273.15) - 14.8435, which is only three arithmetic operations and avoids all linearization error across the target range.","If the linear form is kept, add a note that the linear approximation is itself good to about ±0.03 pK units across 15-35°C, and the full formula should be preferred if the temperature range expands.","The same erroneous -0.0238 coefficient likely appears in the bead description/backlog comment (tanksim-6e5.4.1 comments from 2026-03-26 13:46 UTC). Update that comment to prevent future confusion if the bead is referenced again."],"outcome":"request_changes"},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"0188bb73-0348-4200-8d90-fa98c433e8bc"}
